1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,150
Good morning and welcome, everybody.

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:07,800
I'm Jenny Stewart and I'm the Staff Manager here at the exhibition centre.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:14,616
We're expecting this year's International Travel Exhibition to attract over 10,000 visitors a day, ladies

4
00:00:14,616 --> 00:00:15,919
and gentlemen,

5
00:00:15,919 --> 00:00:20,570
and you are among the two hundred extra staff recruited to help look after

6
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:20,620
them.

7
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:27,130
Now, to help things run smoothly, we have divided you into four teams-the blue

8
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:29,277
team, the green team, the red team,

9
00:00:29,277 --> 00:00:30,200
and the yellow team.

10
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,517
So first I'll explain how the teams are divided up,

11
00:00:34,517 --> 00:00:39,738
and then we'll be giving you colour-coded T-shirts so we can identify you more

12
00:00:39,738 --> 00:00:40,220
easily.

13
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:44,077
First of all, those who will be looking after the phones

14
00:00:44,077 --> 00:00:49,340
and handling all calls regarding the exhibition, you will be on the red team.

15
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:53,318
Now, we've also put the entrance staff on the red team

16
00:00:53,318 --> 00:00:58,420
and you'll be stamping the entrance tickets and giving out publicity leaflets, OK?

17
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:03,230
Those of you involved in distributing entrance tickets will be on the yellow team

18
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:07,660
and we've also put those of you who'll be staffing the information booths around

19
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:09,824
the conference centre on the yellow team,

20
00:01:09,824 --> 00:01:12,430
so you'll be getting a yellow T-shirt.

21
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:17,799
Now, most of the hospitality staff have been put in the blue team,

22
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:22,166
so the chefs among you and the kitchen hands will all need a blue

23
00:01:22,166 --> 00:01:22,787
T-shirt,

24
00:01:22,787 --> 00:01:22,987
but,

25
00:01:22,987 --> 00:01:28,556
because of the sheer numbers, all waiting staff will be on the yellow team,

26
00:01:28,556 --> 00:01:31,020
and this includes the bar staff among you.

27
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:36,277
Those who will be monitoring and directing the traffic in the car parks are

28
00:01:36,277 --> 00:01:37,301
on the green team,

29
00:01:37,301 --> 00:01:40,070
so you'll need to get a green T-shirt.

30
00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:46,193
This year we've also employed a considerable number of attendants to direct the human

31
00:01:46,193 --> 00:01:48,000
traffic around the conference centre.

32
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,833
Now, you'll be working in the exhibition hall at all times, giving directions

33
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:56,599
and generally helping people whenever you can,

34
00:01:56,599 --> 00:01:59,104
and you will be in the red team,

35
00:01:59,104 --> 00:02:01,770
so please collect a red T-shirt.

36
00:02:01,770 --> 00:02:08,341
Right, now that everyone knows what team they're in, we'll get on with the orientation

37
00:02:08,341 --> 00:02:13,370
and training programmer and first I'll run through the rest of today's programme,

38
00:02:13,370 --> 00:02:15,213
which you should have in front of you,

39
00:02:15,213 --> 00:02:18,619
so that you can get a general idea of what else is in store

40
00:02:18,619 --> 00:02:19,000
today.

41
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:25,970
This introduction finishes at 9.30 and then you'll be hearing from Anne Smith.

42
00:02:25,970 --> 00:02:31,784
Anne works in the accounts department on level two and she looks after all

43
00:02:31,784 --> 00:02:33,007
temporary staff,

44
00:02:33,007 --> 00:02:38,079
and so she is the person to see if you have any problems regarding

45
00:02:38,079 --> 00:02:38,700
pay.

46
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:42,740
Anne will be explaining when and how you get this.

47
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,080
She will also be handing out your tax forms.

48
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:51,516
And I will just stress that all tax forms must be completed

49
00:02:51,516 --> 00:02:55,970
and returned to Anne before your pay can be processed.

50
00:02:55,970 --> 00:03:01,929
Following Anne's talk you'll hear from Peter Chen, our Conference Manager,

51
00:03:01,929 --> 00:03:05,842
and he will be going over a plan of the conference centre with you,

52
00:03:05,842 --> 00:03:08,290
which will help you to orient yourselves.

53
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:12,147
He will also go through the security arrangements with you

54
00:03:12,147 --> 00:03:14,960
and show you the fire exits.

55
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:21,162
Then at 10.30, there will be a coffee break in the staff canteen,

56
00:03:21,162 --> 00:03:23,310
which is located down on the ground floor.

57
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:29,964
Now, after the break we'll be moving to a different location for a video

58
00:03:29,964 --> 00:03:30,765
presentation,

59
00:03:30,765 --> 00:03:36,397
so instead of coming back here, we'd like you all to go to Lecture

60
00:03:36,397 --> 00:03:38,000
Room three-one-one.

61
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,314
You'll find it on this same level, just down the hall,

62
00:03:42,314 --> 00:03:47,290
and there you will be shown a video about important safety issues in the

63
00:03:47,290 --> 00:03:50,300
workplace, called Safety at Work.

64
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:53,148
We'll finish off the morning with lunch,

65
00:03:53,148 --> 00:03:57,280
which should give everyone a chance to meet and get to know each other,

66
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:00,730
and we'll be serving you a buffet lunch in the Main Hall,

67
00:04:00,730 --> 00:04:04,140
which is on the first floor, from 12.00 o'clock.

68
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:09,394
After lunch you'll be divided up into your teams to meet your team leaders

69
00:04:09,394 --> 00:04:14,267
and we're hoping to be all finished by 3.00 so I won't delay you

70
00:04:14,267 --> 00:04:14,869
any longer,

71
00:04:14,869 --> 00:04:15,270
and I'll hand over to...
